  "scope": "Original iPhone prng_seedctl runs through actual APFS/VFS and VirtIO-backed Data. Each save passes file/directory fsync and F_FULLFSYNC. The VM is killed without guest shutdown, the saved regular-file overlay is independently read, and a fresh VM reads those exact private bytes through the original utility. Seed bytes and seed digests are never published. This qualifies the VM file-backed path, not physical UFS durability, power-loss atomicity during O_TRUNC/write, hardware entropy quality or hardware data protection."
